    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize explanations (e.g., explain proofs differently per student) or generate adaptive exercises. For example: A chatbot might prompt ‘Try this step-by-step, then reverse-engineer it’—bridging theory with intuition. Risk: Overemphasis on computation over deep understanding."
